  "_note": "The mix (src/audio/audio_mix.gd; docs/KLANG-KONZEPT.de.md section 3). buses: created at start in this order under Master (a bus only sends to one listed before it); volume_db is the bus base level, the player's sliders scale them (Gesamt = Master, Musik = Music and Ambience, Effekte = SFX and UI). Levels of the sound groups stay on the categories (bus base 0 dB except Far), so a category moved to its own bus keeps its old height. effects: added once per bus by id (reverb, lowpass, highpass, compressor); the reverbs take their room from spaces[world] when a story world loads (dry 1, wet per bus); the effects with id muffle are the low-pass the hero's gas or steam drives (filters.gas, cutoff from open_hz towards the gas's Hz by the vision value 0..1). ducks: sidechain compressors - every listed bus gets quieter while the key bus sounds (threshold dB, ratio; depth noted for a key at about -12 dBFS). limiter keeps the Master below ceiling_db. Loudness target in the game (PC): -16 LUFS integrated over a 10-minute session, true peak <= -1 dBTP; the files are levelled by audio_library.json gain_db (sound designer). categories: every sound event names one; it decides the bus and a level in dB. Final level of a sound = base_db + category volume_db + event volume_db + the file's gain_db.",
